{"task_id": "Mbpp/94", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Tuple\n\ndef index_minimum(items: List[Tuple[Any, Any]]) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a list of tuples, returns the first value of the tuple with the smallest second value.\n    If multiple tuples share the same minimal second value, the first encountered is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The built-in min function, with a key, efficiently finds the tuple with the minimum second element.\n    # It also correctly handles ties by returning the first matching item found.\n    min_tuple = min(items, key=lambda x: x[1])\n    return min_tuple[0]"}
