{"task_id": "Mbpp/128", "solution": "def long_words(n, words):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a list of words longer than n characters.\n\n    Parameters:\n    - n (int): threshold length (must be non-negative integer)\n    - words (str | Iterable[str]): input text or iterable of word tokens\n\n    Behavior:\n    - If `words` is a string, it's split on whitespace into tokens.\n    - Leading/trailing punctuation is stripped from each token.\n    - Hyphenated words are treated as single tokens.\n    - Returns tokens (after stripping) whose length is strictly greater than n,\n      preserving original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    import string\n\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer\")\n\n    # Normalize input to an iterable of tokens\n    if isinstance(words, str):\n        raw_tokens = words.split()\n    elif isinstance(words, (list, tuple)):\n        raw_tokens = list(words)\n    else:\n        # Accept any iterable of strings as well\n        try:\n            iter(words)\n            raw_tokens = list(words)\n        except TypeError:\n            raise TypeError(\"words must be a string or an iterable of strings\")\n\n    result = []\n    for token in raw_tokens:\n        if not isinstance(token, str):\n            # Skip non-string entries (be permissive), or alternatively raise\n            continue\n        # Strip leading/trailing punctuation characters\n        normalized = token.strip(string.punctuation)\n        if not normalized:\n            continue\n        # Ensure token contains at least one alphanumeric character\n        if not any(ch.isalnum() for ch in normalized):\n            continue\n        if len(normalized) > n:\n            result.append(normalized)\n    return result"}
