{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest unique items from the input list.\n    Uses heapq.nlargest for efficient retrieval of the top items.\n    \"\"\"\n    import heapq\n\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"input_list must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer\")\n\n    unique_items = list(set(input_list))\n    # heapq.nlargest returns items in descending order\n    largest_n = heapq.nlargest(n, unique_items)\n    return largest_n"}
