{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of sequences of length n, where each element is a positive integer,\n    is greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and is less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(m, int) or not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"m and n must be integers\")\n    if m < 1 or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"m and n must be positive integers (>= 1)\")\n\n    # Base case: length 1 -> any integer 1..m\n    prev_dp = [0] * (m + 1)         # dp values for previous length (index 0 unused)\n    prev_prefix_sum = [0] * (m + 1) # prefix sums of prev_dp\n\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        prev_dp[j] = 1\n        prev_prefix_sum[j] = prev_prefix_sum[j - 1] + prev_dp[j]\n\n    # Build up to length n\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        current_dp = [0] * (m + 1)\n        current_prefix_sum = [0] * (m + 1)\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            max_prev = j // 2\n            if max_prev >= 1:\n                current_dp[j] = prev_prefix_sum[max_prev]\n            else:\n                current_dp[j] = 0\n            current_prefix_sum[j] = current_prefix_sum[j - 1] + current_dp[j]\n        prev_dp = current_dp\n        prev_prefix_sum = current_prefix_sum\n\n    return prev_prefix_sum[m]"}
