{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(list_of_tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique, canonicalized 2-element tuples in a list.\n    Unordered pairs (a, b) and (b, a) are considered identical and canonicalized to a deterministic ordering.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n\n    def _canonicalize_pair(pair):\n        \"\"\"\n        Canonicalizes a 2-element pair into a consistent tuple.\n        Handles unorderable types by using their string representation for comparison.\n        Raises ValueError if the input is not a 2-element iterable.\n        \"\"\"\n        try:\n            a, b = pair\n        except Exception:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each item must be a 2-element iterable (e.g., tuple/list of length 2)\")\n        try:\n            ordered_pair = tuple(sorted((a, b)))\n        except TypeError:\n            ordered_pair = tuple(sorted((a, b), key=lambda x: repr(x)))\n        return ordered_pair\n\n    for item in list_of_tuples:\n        canonical_pair = _canonicalize_pair(item)\n        counts[canonical_pair] = counts.get(canonical_pair, 0) + 1\n\n    return counts"}
