{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than a given non-negative integer n\n    using the Sieve of Eratosthenes algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n\n    sieve = [True] * n\n    sieve[0] = sieve[1] = False\n    p = 2\n    while p * p < n:\n        if sieve[p]:\n            for multiple in range(p * p, n, p):\n                sieve[multiple] = False\n        p += 1\n\n    return sum(1 for flag in sieve if flag)"}
