{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit's value.\n    Handles negative numbers by considering their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\n    s = str(abs(n))\n    digit_counts = {}\n    for char_digit in s:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        if digit == 0:\n            return False  # If digit '0' appears, frequency >= 1 > 0, so return False.\n        digit_counts[digit] = digit_counts.get(digit, 0) + 1\n\n    for digit, count in digit_counts.items():\n        if count > digit:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
