{"task_id": "Mbpp/281", "solution": "from typing import Any, Callable, Iterable, Optional, Set, List\n\ndef all_unique(iterable: Iterable[Any], key: Optional[Callable[[Any], Any]] = None, allow_unhashable: bool = True) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in an iterable are unique.\n    Supports optional key function and handling of unhashable elements.\n\n    Behavior:\n    - If an element (or its key) is hashable, uniqueness is checked via its hash.\n    - If an element (or its key) is unhashable and allow_unhashable is True, falls back to equality comparisons.\n    - If an element (or its key) is unhashable and allow_unhashable is False, returns False (cannot verify uniqueness).\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_hashes: Set[int] = set()\n    seen_unhashable: List[Any] = []\n\n    for item in iterable:\n        key_val = key(item) if key else item\n\n        try:\n            h = hash(key_val)\n            if h in seen_hashes:\n                return False\n            seen_hashes.add(h)\n        except TypeError:\n            if allow_unhashable:\n                for s in seen_unhashable:\n                    if s == key_val:\n                        return False\n                seen_unhashable.append(key_val)\n            else:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
