{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(values, *, coerce_numeric_strings: bool = False, ignore_booleans: bool = True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the minimum numeric value found in the iterable `values`.\n    Non-numeric items are ignored. By default strings are ignored; set\n    coerce_numeric_strings=True to attempt parsing numeric strings.\n    Booleans are ignored by default (ignore_booleans=True) because bool is a\n    subclass of int in Python; set ignore_booleans=False to include them.\n    Raises ValueError if no numeric value is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    from decimal import Decimal\n    from fractions import Fraction\n\n    numeric_types = (int, float, Decimal, Fraction)\n\n    best = None\n    for item in values:\n        num = None\n\n        # Handle booleans explicitly because isinstance(True, int) is True\n        if isinstance(item, bool):\n            if ignore_booleans:\n                continue\n            num = int(item)\n        # Direct numeric types\n        elif isinstance(item, numeric_types):\n            num = item\n        # Optionally coerce numeric strings\n        elif coerce_numeric_strings and isinstance(item, str):\n            s = item.strip()\n            if not s:\n                continue\n            # Try int, then float, then Decimal, then Fraction\n            try:\n                # Allow leading +/-\n                if '.' in s or 'e' in s.lower():\n                    num = float(s)\n                else:\n                    num = int(s)\n            except Exception:\n                try:\n                    num = float(s)\n                except Exception:\n                    try:\n                        num = Decimal(s)\n                    except Exception:\n                        try:\n                            num = Fraction(s)\n                        except Exception:\n                            continue\n        else:\n            continue\n\n        # Maintain running minimum, with a safe fallback comparison\n        if best is None:\n            best = num\n        else:\n            try:\n                if num < best:\n                    best = num\n            except TypeError:\n                # Fallback: compare by converting to float (best-effort)\n                try:\n                    if float(num) < float(best):\n                        best = num\n                except Exception:\n                    raise TypeError(\"Cannot compare numeric types found in the input.\")\n\n    if best is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No numeric values found in the input.\")\n\n    return best"}
