{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(*lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes duplicate numbers from a given number of lists, returning only those that appear exactly once.\n    The order of the unique numbers is preserved based on their first appearance across all input lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    flattened_items = []\n    for sublist in lists:\n        for item in sublist:\n            flattened_items.append(item)\n\n    counts = {}\n    for item in flattened_items:\n        counts[item] = counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    result = []\n    for item in flattened_items:\n        if counts[item] == 1:\n            result.append(item)\n    return result"}
