{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\ndef merge(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list of two-element sublists into two separate lists.\n    The first output list contains all first elements, the second all second elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_elements: List[Any] = []\n    second_elements: List[Any] = []\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        first_elements.append(sublist[0])\n        second_elements.append(sublist[1])\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "def div_list(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Divide two lists element-wise and return a list of floats.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: if the input lists have different lengths.\n        TypeError: if any element cannot be converted to float.\n        ZeroDivisionError: if any divisor is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lists must have the same length\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i, (x, y) in enumerate(zip(a, b)):\n        try:\n            nx = float(x)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Invalid numerator at index {i}: {x!r}\")\n        try:\n            ny = float(y)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Invalid denominator at index {i}: {y!r}\")\n        if ny == 0.0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(f\"Division by zero at index {i}\")\n        result.append(nx / ny)\n    return result"}
