{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "solution": "def move_num(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Moves all contiguous digit sequences to the end of the string, preserving relative order.\n\n    Non-digit characters also maintain their relative order at the beginning.\n    \"\"\"\n    non_digits_parts = []\n    digit_groups = []\n    current_digits = []\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            current_digits.append(char)\n        else:\n            if current_digits:\n                digit_groups.append(\"\".join(current_digits))\n                current_digits = []\n            non_digits_parts.append(char)\n\n    if current_digits:\n        digit_groups.append(\"\".join(current_digits))\n\n    return \"\".join(non_digits_parts) + \"\".join(digit_groups)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size using a divide-and-conquer approach.\n    Assumes n >= 1 and lists are sorted in non-decreasing order.\n    Returns a float.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def find_median_recursive(ar1, ar2, low1, high1, low2, high2):\n        k = high1 - low1 + 1  # current size of subarrays\n\n        # Base cases\n        if k == 1:\n            return (float(ar1[low1]) + ar2[low2]) / 2.0\n        if k == 2:\n            return (float(max(ar1[low1], ar2[low2])) + min(ar1[high1], ar2[high2])) / 2.0\n\n        # Middle indices\n        mid1 = low1 + (k - 1) // 2\n        mid2 = low2 + (k - 1) // 2\n\n        m1 = ar1[mid1]\n        m2 = ar2[mid2]\n\n        if m1 == m2:\n            return float(m1)\n        elif m1 < m2:\n            # Discard first half of ar1 and second half of ar2\n            return find_median_recursive(ar1, ar2, mid1, high1, low2, mid2)\n        else:\n            # Discard second half of ar1 and first half of ar2\n            return find_median_recursive(ar1, ar2, low1, mid1, mid2, high2)\n\n    return find_median_recursive(list1, list2, 0, n - 1, 0, n - 1)"}
