{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(grid: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average path in a square matrix from top-left to bottom-right,\n    moving only right or down. This is equivalent to finding the maximum sum path.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(grid)\n\n    # dp[r][c] stores the maximum sum to reach cell (r, c)\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Initialize the starting cell\n    dp[0][0] = float(grid[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row (only right moves possible)\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c - 1] + float(grid[0][c])\n\n    # Fill the first column (only down moves possible)\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r - 1][0] + float(grid[r][0])\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            # To reach (r, c), choose the path from (r-1, c) or (r, c-1)\n            # that yields the maximum sum\n            dp[r][c] = max(dp[r - 1][c], dp[r][c - 1]) + float(grid[r][c])\n\n    # The maximum sum to reach the bottom-right cell\n    max_total_sum = dp[n - 1][n - 1]\n\n    # The number of cells in any path from top-left to bottom-right\n    # in an N*N grid, moving only right or down, is always 2*N - 1.\n    path_length = 2 * n - 1\n\n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_average = max_total_sum / path_length\n\n    return max_average"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "solution": "def power_base_sum(base, power):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all digits of the base raised to the specified power.\n    Assumes valid integer inputs are provided per design context.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = base ** power\n    return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(abs(result)))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/722", "solution": "def filter_data(records: dict, min_height: float, min_weight: float) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters student records, keeping only those where both height and weight\n    are strictly greater than the specified minimums.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_students = {}\n    for name, (height, weight) in records.items():\n        if height > min_height and weight > min_weight:\n            filtered_students[name] = (height, weight)\n    return filtered_students"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "import re\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef extract_quotation(text: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts values between double quotation marks from the given string.\n    Escaped double quotes (\\\") and backslashes (\\\\) within the content are unescaped.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _unescape_content(s: str) -> str:\n        # Convert escaped backslashes first, then escaped quotes.\n        s = s.replace('\\\\\\\\', '\\\\')\n        s = s.replace('\\\\\"', '\"')\n        return s\n\n    # Regex pattern to match content inside double quotes,\n    # ensuring the opening quote is not escaped and handling escaped characters within.\n    # Group 1 captures the content between the quotes.\n    REGEX_PATTERN = r'(?<!\\\\)\"((?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*)\"'\n    _compiled_regex = re.compile(REGEX_PATTERN)\n\n    extracted_values: List[str] = []\n    for match in _compiled_regex.finditer(text):\n        raw_content = match.group(1)\n        unescaped_content = _unescape_content(raw_content)\n        extracted_values.append(unescaped_content)\n\n    return extracted_values"}
