{"task_id": "Mbpp/726", "solution": "def multiply_elements(t):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of adjacent elements in a tuple of numbers.\n    The returned tuple has a length of N, where the i-th element is t_i * t_{i+1}.\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(t[i] * t[i+1] for i in range(len(t) - 1))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/730", "solution": "from typing import Sequence, List, Any, TypeVar\n\nT = TypeVar(\"T\")\n\ndef consecutive_duplicates(items: Sequence[T]) -> List[T]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes consecutive duplicate elements from a list-like sequence.\n    Preserves the order of elements and keeps non-consecutive duplicates.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Inline helper function for safe equality comparison.\n    def _safe_eq(a: Any, b: Any) -> bool:\n        try:\n            return a == b\n        except Exception:\n            return False\n\n    result: List[T] = []\n    # Use a unique sentinel object for initial comparison to ensure the first item is always added.\n    prev_item: Any = object()\n\n    for item in items:\n        if not _safe_eq(item, prev_item):\n            result.append(item)\n        prev_item = item\n\n    return result"}
