{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(seq, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the leftmost index at which `value` should be inserted in `seq`\n    to maintain sorted (non-decreasing) order.\n\n    Accepts a Sequence or any iterable (will be converted to a list).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure we have random access; convert non-sequence iterables to list\n    if not hasattr(seq, \"__len__\") or not hasattr(seq, \"__getitem__\"):\n        seq = list(seq)\n\n    low, high = 0, len(seq)\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if seq[mid] < value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "import math\n\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer >= 1\")\n\n    # The smallest n-digit number is 10^(n-1).\n    target = 10 ** (n - 1)\n\n    # Solve k*(k+1)/2 >= target -> k^2 + k - 2*target >= 0\n    # Positive root: k = (-1 + sqrt(1 + 8*target)) / 2\n    # Smallest integer k is ceil of that root.\n\n    discriminant = 1 + 8 * target\n    s = math.isqrt(discriminant)  # floor(sqrt(discriminant))\n\n    # Compute ceil((-1 + s) / 2) with integer arithmetic\n    num = s - 1\n    k = num // 2\n    if num % 2 != 0:\n        k += 1\n\n    return k"}
